    {
      "block_id": "2605.28896_p1_b6",
      "text": "Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) has emerged as a widely adopted approach for adapting\nlarge language models, yet the internal representational changes induced by LoRA fine-\ntuning remain insufficiently understood.\nIn this work, we investigate the geometry of\nLoRA-induced representations using Sparse Autoencoders (SAEs). We introduce a delta\nactivation framework that isolates the adapter-specific contribution to the residual stream as\n",
      "bbox": [
        99.27,
        318.03,
        497.7,
        375.8
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        397,
        1272,
        1990,
