      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.28896_p1_b11",
      "text": "Large language models (LLMs) are increasingly deployed not as base models but as fine-tuned\nvariants, with LoRA [Hu et al., 2022] being the dominant adaptation method. LoRA constrains\nweight updates to a low-rank factorization \u2206W = BA where B \u2208Rd\u00d7r and A \u2208Rr\u00d7d, with\nrank r \u226ad. Despite its widespread use in instruction tuning, domain adaptation, and safety\nalignment, almost nothing is understood about what LoRA does to a model\u2019s internal feature\ngeometry.\n",
      "bbox": [
        71.25,
        633.96,
        523.75,
        712.62
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        285,
        2535,
        2094,
