      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.91,
      "font_name": "CMR10",
      "is_math": true,
      "char_count": 458,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.28896_p1_b12",
      "text": "The mechanistic interpretability literature has made substantial progress in characterizing\nbase model representations using Sparse Autoencoders [Bricken et al., 2023, Templeton et\nal., 2024], which decompose superposed residual stream activations into sparse, approximately\nmonosemantic feature directions. However, this toolkit has been applied almost exclusively\n",
